+# JSON utility
 
-Use `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin. Existing action: read. Domain functions accept the payload object; api.dispatch routes it. CLI reports ValueError/KeyError with stderr and exit 2.
+Use `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin; one JSON result is printed on stdout.
+ValueError/KeyError are reported on stderr with exit code 2 (no traceback).
+
+Actions (routed through `api.dispatch(payload)`):
+
+- `read`: keys `action`, `records`, `id`. Returns a deep copy of the record
+  (`{version, data}`) or `null` when the id is missing.
+- `update`: keys `action`, `records`, `id`, `expected` (null or nonnegative int),
+  `patch` (JSON object). One compare-and-set transaction:
+  - `expected` null: create-only. If `id` is absent, creates `{version: 1, data: patch}`;
+    if present, rejected (never an unconditional overwrite).
+  - `expected` equals the record's current version: shallow-merges `patch` keys into
+    `data` (null patch values are stored, not deleted) and increments `version` by 1.
+  - otherwise rejected.
+  Returns `{applied: bool, records: <new independent object>, record: <independent record or null>}`.
+  Inputs are never mutated; all returned nested containers are independent of the input
+  and `record` is independent of the returned `records`.
